# Bulk ANI datasets (93MB) — fetched by ./download-assets.sh, not tracked
# in git. Small essential inputs (the cholesterol-family .xyz / .gjf.log
# files) are intentionally NOT listed here and stay tracked, the same way
# TorchANI tracks its small test .pdb files but ignores *.h5/*.hdf5.
/data/*.h5
/data/*.hdf5

# Model checkpoints: the pretrained starting point and the checkpoints
# produced by running 01_transfer_learning/. Fetched by
# ./download-assets.sh; scripts also add to this directory when run.
/model/

# Per-epoch training logs and aggregated RMSE pickles: regenerated by
# running the scripts, or fetched pre-computed by ./download-assets.sh.
/results/
/02_ani_dataset_results/*.pickle

# Generated figures
/02_ani_dataset_results/out/
/03_cholesterol_validation/out/

# PBS job scripts tied to the specific HPC cluster these were run on
# (queue names, module versions, a venv path local to that machine) —
# not portable, and not needed to run anything above (see README.md).
# download-assets.sh is the one generic entry-point script and is kept.
*.sh
!/download-assets.sh

# Python cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints/
